   'Deep Learning',
   'Four levels, twelve lessons, from one neuron to a transformer',
   'Deep learning is machine learning with models that learn their own features. A traditional model needs you to tell it that recency matters and that price divided by tenure is informative; a neural network, given enough examples, works out its own intermediate representations from raw input.

That is why it took over the problems where features are impossible to write down by hand. Nobody can specify the rule that distinguishes a cat from a dog in pixel values, or what makes a sentence sarcastic. Images, audio and language are where deep learning is not just better but the only thing that works.

